WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:01.699
All right, welcome back to the show.

00:00:01.699 --> 00:00:03.710
Let's let's hear from some folks.

00:00:03.710 --> 00:00:10.050
It is the, I guess, sort of Thanksgiving edition
of live calls hitting us earlier this week

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:15.260
because we will be off on Thursday and Friday
for the Thanksgiving holiday.

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:22.929
We are taking calls via discord at David Pakman
dot com slash discord, discourse, c, o, r,

00:00:22.929 --> 00:00:29.710
d and we have all sorts of different people
who are interested in chatting today.

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:31.199
Let's start with Andrew.

00:00:31.199 --> 00:00:32.279
From Miami.

00:00:32.279 --> 00:00:33.279
Andrew from Miami.

00:00:33.279 --> 00:00:34.279
You're on the air.

00:00:34.279 --> 00:00:36.480
Hi, David, how's it going, hear me?

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:37.719
Yes, I can.

00:00:37.719 --> 00:00:43.600
Great, I was wondering what your opinion was
of remember when Bloomberg banned Democratic

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:44.600
primary?

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:45.600
Yeah.

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:47.230
He threw in like a billion dollars or something,
right?

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:52.670
I think it was I think it was a hundred and
fifty or two hundred million, certainly.

00:00:52.670 --> 00:00:58.300
Oh, no, I think reporting from Washington
Post, New York Times said it was around 900

00:00:58.300 --> 00:00:59.300
million.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:00.300
Oh, maybe it is.

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:01.309
Yeah, I'm not saying you're wrong.

00:01:01.309 --> 00:01:04.040
I had not heard that number, but it's conceivable.

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:05.360
Sure.

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:10.720
And then during the actual presidential election,
you went through in about hundred million

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:13.790
in one state.

00:01:13.790 --> 00:01:18.780
I found that interesting because he said that
Trump was an existential threat, secrecy and

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:23.649
didn't, and I think he said he was going to
do like everything possible to get Biden elected

00:01:23.649 --> 00:01:24.649
and he didn't.

00:01:24.649 --> 00:01:27.750
I mean, listen, 100 million is nothing to
sneeze at, obviously.

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:34.659
But for a guy with his wealth, he could certainly
have have put in way more.

00:01:34.659 --> 00:01:37.840
For sure, and I think that's why people are
saying things like, you know, eat the rich

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:42.650
and whatnot, but I mean, I also saw even on
the Democratic side, like Obama only came

00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:47.880
out around two or three weeks before the election
and then afterward, he has this book tour

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:49.479
where he's on every major news station.

00:01:49.479 --> 00:01:50.820
Isn't that pretty interesting?

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:54.049
Yeah, I'm I find the Obama thing less surprising.

00:01:54.049 --> 00:01:59.340
I mean, I think during the primary, Obama's
approach was clearer, which was he's not going

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:04.219
to get involved close to the primary or before
it's decided because he wants to be able to

00:02:04.219 --> 00:02:06.460
credibly support whoever the nominee is.

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:10.119
And if he ends up, you know, endorsing someone
during the primary who doesn't end up being

00:02:10.119 --> 00:02:13.150
the nominee, it could just hurt his ability
to campaign for them.

00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:18.790
If you're right, that Obama was only on the
physical campaign trail for a couple of weeks.

00:02:18.790 --> 00:02:24.319
But I think a lot of that was that there was
really no in-person campaigning being done

00:02:24.319 --> 00:02:27.440
on the Democratic side for a while because
of the virus.

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:32.480
He you know, Obama did speak at the DNC, which
was remote.

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:34.010
That's less of a flag to me.

00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:37.370
The Bloomberg thing, it's just like he was
obviously just dishonest about how involved

00:02:37.370 --> 00:02:40.090
he was going to be and helping the eventual
nominee win.

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:41.820
He just lied.

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:43.819
Right, definitely cool.

00:02:43.819 --> 00:02:45.490
Yeah, thanks for taking my question.

00:02:45.490 --> 00:02:46.490
Appreciate it.

00:02:46.490 --> 00:03:33.129
All right, Andrew from Miami, great to hear

00:03:33.129 --> 00:04:12.400
from you.

